# Karpathy Auditor - V21_QUANT Compliant (karpathy-auditor v2.1)
**Version:** V21_QUANT-Compliant

## Code Auditing Skill for V21_QUANT Project

This skill provides systematic code auditing with mandatory /ac (Codex Audit) integration and Institutional Grade standards compliance.

---

## Audit Workflow

### Phase 1: Pre-Audit Preparation
1. Verify code follows OpenClaw naming conventions
2. Check Institutional Grade standards compliance
3. Review Vectorization implementation
4. Validate PIT (Proper Input Typing) compliance

### Phase 2: Code Analysis
- Analyze diff against base branch
- Check SQL safety
- Verify LLM trust boundary violations
- Review conditional side effects
- Validate structural integrity

### Phase 3: Audit Documentation
- **Mandatory:** All findings logged in /ac (Codex Audit) system
- Document all security concerns
- Record compliance status
- Generate audit report

### Phase 4: Verification
- Ensure all changes have corresponding /ac entries
- Verify Vectorization standards met
- Confirm PIT compliance
- Validate Institutional Grade requirements

---

## Institutional Grade Standards

### Vectorization Requirements
- Prioritize vectorized operations over iterative solutions
- Use numpy/pandas vectorization where applicable
- Benchmark performance improvements
- Document vectorization strategy in /ac

### PIT Compliance (Proper Input Typing)
- All function parameters must have type annotations
- Input validation at API boundaries
- Type checking for all external inputs
- Document typing decisions in audit log

---

## /ac (Codex Audit) Integration

### Mandatory Audit Trail
Every coding session must include:
1. **Start Audit:** Log session start with timestamp
2. **Change Log:** Document each modification with rationale
3. **Compliance Check:** Verify V21_QUANT standards
4. **End Audit:** Final verification and sign-off

### Audit Entry Format
```
/ac entry {
  timestamp: "2026-04-23T12:00:00Z",
  change: "description of change",
  rationale: "why this change was necessary",
  compliance: ["Vectorization", "PIT", "OpenClaw naming"],
  review_status: "pending|approved|rejected"
}
```

---

## Verification Checklist

**Pre-Deployment Audit:**
- [ ] All code changes logged in /ac
- [ ] Vectorization standards applied
- [ ] PIT compliance verified
- [ ] OpenClaw naming conventions followed
- [ ] Institutional Grade standards met
- [ ] Audit trail complete and verifiable

**Post-Deployment Review:**
- [ ] Production monitoring active
- [ ] Performance benchmarks recorded
- [ ] Audit trail accessible
- [ ] Compliance report generated

---

## Usage Guidelines

**When to Use:**
- Before any production code changes
- During code review sessions
- When validating third-party integrations
- For compliance reporting

**Integration Points:**
- All coding workflows must include /ac audit steps
- Use this skill to validate Institutional Grade compliance
- Reference this skill in all PR descriptions
- Link to specific /ac audit entries in commit messages

**V21_QUANT Specific Requirements:**
- All work must reference corresponding /ac entries
- Changes must meet Vectorization standards
- PIT compliance is mandatory
- Documentation must be updated in AUDIT.md

