.ly_state/session\audit_reports\role21_p9_dynamic_rebalance_audit_20260609.md:1:# L3 Audit Report - P9 Dynamic Rebalance Frequency
.ly_state/session\audit_reports\role21_p9_dynamic_rebalance_audit_20260609.md:5:Scope: Audit P9 dynamic rebalance implementation in `src/omega/quant/phase35_walk_forward.py`.
.ly_state/session\audit_reports\role21_p9_dynamic_rebalance_audit_20260609.md:23:- Checked P9 v3 evidence log `.ly_state/session/p9_fixed_v3_backtest_20260609.log`.
.ly_state/session\audit_reports\role21_p9_dynamic_rebalance_audit_20260609.md:24:- Checked P8 baseline report `.ly_state/session/P8_FINAL_REPORT.md`.
.ly_state/session\audit_reports\role21_p9_dynamic_rebalance_audit_20260609.md:35:This means day 1 of a test fold can receive a rebalance cadence chosen using volatility from later test dates, including the final rolling 20-day window of the fold. That is not PIT-safe. Sorting by ticker/date, clipping returns, and using train-only baseline volatility are correct hygiene, but they do not remove the future-test information used in `current_vol`.
.ly_state/session\audit_reports\role21_p9_dynamic_rebalance_audit_20260609.md:37:Required fix: replace the fold-level detector with a sequential detector. For each rebalance decision date, compute baseline from `train_df` plus only prior available test bars, never from current/future test bars. Acceptable pattern:
.ly_state/session\audit_reports\role21_p9_dynamic_rebalance_audit_20260609.md:39:- Before first OOS bar: use train-only baseline/default cadence.
.ly_state/session\audit_reports\role21_p9_dynamic_rebalance_audit_20260609.md:54:P9 v3 metrics from evidence:
.ly_state/session\audit_reports\role21_p9_dynamic_rebalance_audit_20260609.md:59:- Average Portfolio Sharpe: 1.0121
.ly_state/session\audit_reports\role21_p9_dynamic_rebalance_audit_20260609.md:62:P8 baseline:
.ly_state/session\audit_reports\role21_p9_dynamic_rebalance_audit_20260609.md:65:- Average Portfolio Sharpe: 0.90
.ly_state/session\audit_reports\role21_p9_dynamic_rebalance_audit_20260609.md:68:Sharpe improves by about 12.5% and MaxDD improves by 0.65 percentage points, but Portfolio IC drops from 0.0120 to 0.0020. That is an 83.3% degradation in predictive alignment. More importantly, the risk metrics are contaminated by fold-level lookahead, so they cannot justify approval. Even after a PIT-safe sequential fix, this tradeoff should be re-run and compared against P8 before merge.
