.ly_state/session\audit_reports\role23_p10_performance_rebuttal_20260609.md:16:P10 is not cleared as a performance improvement. The implementation blends horizons, but current evidence does not prove additive signal versus P9, does not provide comparable official full-backtest metrics, and has weight logic that can assign large positive weight to horizons whose validation IC is negative. The quick smoke all-zero metrics are explainable by a one-symbol universe, but that also means the smoke is not performance evidence.
.ly_state/session\audit_reports\role23_p10_performance_rebuttal_20260609.md:27:- P9: IC `0.0091`, Sharpe `0.9854`, MaxDD `-8.12%`
.ly_state/session\audit_reports\role23_p10_performance_rebuttal_20260609.md:32:- No-save quick backtest comparison: baseline `2.749s`, P10 `4.017s`; both all-zero metrics with `top_n_symbols=1`.
.ly_state/session\audit_reports\role23_p10_performance_rebuttal_20260609.md:37:### 1. No proven performance lift versus P9
.ly_state/session\audit_reports\role23_p10_performance_rebuttal_20260609.md:39:L2 report provides test pass counts but no comparable full P10 backtest against the stated P9 baseline. My no-save full-ish run did not show a convincing lift:
.ly_state/session\audit_reports\role23_p10_performance_rebuttal_20260609.md:41:| Case | Runtime | IC | Raw IC | Daily CS IC | Sharpe | MaxDD |
.ly_state/session\audit_reports\role23_p10_performance_rebuttal_20260609.md:43:| P9 current path, XGBoost flag true | `14.127s` | `-0.00295` | `0.00325` | `0.00604` | `1.6804` | `-67.31%` |
.ly_state/session\audit_reports\role23_p10_performance_rebuttal_20260609.md:45:| P9 no-XGBoost apples-to-apples | `9.359s` | `0.00024` | `0.01105` | `0.01231` | `1.5726` | `-66.49%` |
.ly_state/session\audit_reports\role23_p10_performance_rebuttal_20260609.md:47:P10 raw IC improves slightly versus no-XGBoost, but Sharpe is basically flat and drawdown is worse. Against the supplied P9 baseline, the local run's drawdown regime is not comparable, so this must not be approved without an official full backtest artifact using identical config, data window, universe, costs, Stage2 settings, and target metric definitions.
.ly_state/session\audit_reports\role23_p10_performance_rebuttal_20260609.md:49:### 2. P10 metrics are not comparable to default P9 XGBoost path
.ly_state/session\audit_reports\role23_p10_performance_rebuttal_20260609.md:53:Result: P10 artifacts can say `use_xgboost=true` while the P10 fold path did not use XGBoost. That makes P9/P10 performance claims easy to misread.
.ly_state/session\audit_reports\role23_p10_performance_rebuttal_20260609.md:56:- P9 default XGBoost vs P10 with XGBoost disabled explicitly, clearly labelled; or
.ly_state/session\audit_reports\role23_p10_performance_rebuttal_20260609.md:57:- P10 integrated with XGBoost and compared to P9 default path.
.ly_state/session\audit_reports\role23_p10_performance_rebuttal_20260609.md:78:- Quick mode: P10 `4.017s` vs baseline `2.749s` -> `+46%`.
.ly_state/session\audit_reports\role23_p10_performance_rebuttal_20260609.md:79:- Full-ish XGBoost-flag path: P10 `16.928s` vs current P9 path `14.127s` -> `+20%`.
.ly_state/session\audit_reports\role23_p10_performance_rebuttal_20260609.md:80:- P10 versus no-XGBoost apples-to-apples baseline: `16.928s` vs `9.359s` -> `+81%`.
.ly_state/session\audit_reports\role23_p10_performance_rebuttal_20260609.md:82:The overhead is structurally expected because P10 computes horizon signal selection/gating three times. It is not justified without a clear Sharpe/drawdown/stability gain.
.ly_state/session\audit_reports\role23_p10_performance_rebuttal_20260609.md:93:- P10 improves or at least does not degrade Sharpe/MaxDD versus P9 on a fixed fixture.
.ly_state/session\audit_reports\role23_p10_performance_rebuttal_20260609.md:103:3. Produce official full P9/P10 comparison artifacts with identical config and explicit XGBoost state. Include fold-level IC, raw IC, daily CS IC, Sharpe, MaxDD, turnover/cost, and runtime.
.ly_state/session\audit_reports\role23_p10_performance_rebuttal_20260609.md:104:4. Add a performance regression test or benchmark fixture that fails on Sharpe/drawdown degradation and catches degenerate equal-weight fallback.
.ly_state/session\audit_reports\role23_p10_performance_rebuttal_20260609.md:113:Rebuttal Summary: P10 currently looks like a noisy multi-horizon average with unsafe absolute-IC weighting, incomplete experiment wiring, non-comparable XGBoost behavior, and no full evidence that it beats P9 after costs/drawdown. Quick zero metrics are due to insufficient one-symbol smoke universe, not proof of success or failure.
