.ly_state/session\audit_reports\role23_p10_performance_fix2_reaudit_20260609.md:36:No blocking performance findings remain for P10 as an opt-in experimental feature. P10 is not approved as a default strategy or as a proven performance improvement over P9.
.ly_state/session\audit_reports\role23_p10_performance_fix2_reaudit_20260609.md:48:PASS. The single-horizon guard checks the selected method quality before returning the signal. If `quality_val <= 0`, it returns `None` to trigger baseline fallback at `src/omega/quant/phase35_walk_forward.py:1351` through `src/omega/quant/phase35_walk_forward.py:1360`.
.ly_state/session\audit_reports\role23_p10_performance_fix2_reaudit_20260609.md:66:Residual note: output filenames still use the generic `xgboost`/`baseline` suffix at `scripts/run_phase35_backtest.py:322` through `scripts/run_phase35_backtest.py:330`, so humans must inspect JSON/config or logs before treating an artifact as full P10 evidence. This is not blocking because the quick artifact is machine-labeled and the CLI warning is explicit, but future cleanup should add `quick`/`p10` to filenames or summary headers.
.ly_state/session\audit_reports\role23_p10_performance_fix2_reaudit_20260609.md:72:Documented full comparable P10 evidence: command completed with Portfolio IC `-0.0028`, Raw IC `0.0038`, Raw Daily CS IC `0.0067`, Sharpe `0.9475`, MaxDD `-7.88%`; note says P10 mostly fell back because strict gate excluded all horizons at `.ly_state/session/p10_role21_fix_reaudit_prompt_20260609.md:33` through `.ly_state/session/p10_role21_fix_reaudit_prompt_20260609.md:37`.
.ly_state/session\audit_reports\role23_p10_performance_fix2_reaudit_20260609.md:74:P9 baseline evidence remains IC `0.0091`, Sharpe `0.9854`, MaxDD `-8.12%` at `.ly_state/session/audit_reports/role21_p9_cadence_fix_reaudit_20260609.md:34`.
.ly_state/session\audit_reports\role23_p10_performance_fix2_reaudit_20260609.md:76:Assessment: P10 underperforms P9 on IC and Sharpe, while MaxDD is slightly better. That is not acceptable as proof of improvement and must not be marketed as a production upgrade. It is acceptable for gate approval only because P10 is default-off/opt-in, strict-gate failures fallback to the approved single-horizon baseline, and Role20/Role21 already approved the safety fixes.
.ly_state/session\audit_reports\role23_p10_performance_fix2_reaudit_20260609.md:84:If no horizons pass or all selected quality is non-positive, fallback executes the standard single-horizon baseline at `src/omega/quant/phase35_walk_forward.py:1539` through `src/omega/quant/phase35_walk_forward.py:1581`. This caps behavioral risk: a weak P10 blend does not silently become equal-weight or wrong-way; it falls back. Runtime remains acceptable for experiment use, not for making P10 default without a separate benchmark budget.
.ly_state/session\audit_reports\role23_p10_performance_fix2_reaudit_20260609.md:90:Role23 approves P10 Fix2 performance safety only under these constraints: P10 remains opt-in, quick mode remains smoke-only, and the documented full result is treated as experimental evidence with degradation versus P9, not as a strategy improvement claim.
